  "identifier_convention": {
    "description": "Stable case-sensitive CAIF identifiers use full English book names as frozen registry keys, not localized display labels. Numbered books use an ASCII digit (1, 2, or 3), one ASCII space, and the full name: 1 Samuel, 1 Corinthians, 2 John. No Roman numerals or ordinal words in identifiers. Multiword unnumbered identifiers retain spaces (Song of Songs).",
    "source_selection": "First 66 entries of SIL Canon.AllBookIds and allBookEnglishNames, paired by index. Explicit CAIF naming overrides: EST -> Esther; DAN -> Daniel. These denote the Protestant forms; other future forms require distinct identities when necessary.",
    "stability": "Alias additions do not rename IDs. Object entry order has no canonical meaning. Profile membership and order are defined only in canon-profiles.json."
  },
